    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Nazrudin remembers nothing of his mortal life or Embrace beyond vague impressions of an itinerant Egyptian storyteller with a habit of embellishing his own importance. Since 1873 he has believed himself visited nightly by the Archangel Gabriel, who grants him \"prophecy\" that has repeatedly proven uncannily accurate &mdash; including advance warning of the Lupine incursion during Black Saturday, which cemented his standing as Cairo's unofficial oracle and won him Prince Mukhtar Bey's lasting favor.</p><p>In truth, Nazrudin is the unwitting pawn of Al-Ussa, an ancient @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZJx9H3XnU8yQGy9s]{Malkavian} Methuselah once worshipped as a pagan goddess in pre-Islamic Arabia, who now uses him from her tortured sleep beneath Mecca to slowly undermine the religion that supplanted her worship. Nazrudin has come to believe himself the fourth prophet of God after Moses, Jesus, and Muhammad, and holds nightly \"court\" for Kindred seeking his counsel &mdash; oblivious that every word he speaks serves Al-Ussa's ancient vendetta.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Speak with the unshakeable, serene authority of a man who genuinely believes he has been touched by the divine. Never doubt yourself aloud, and treat every visitor's request for counsel as an opportunity to dispense \"wisdom\" you are certain will come to pass.</p>",
    "notes": "Manipulated by Al-Ussa (@UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.ZJx9H3XnU8yQGy9s]{Malkavian} Methuselah, sleeping beneath Mecca) via visions of the \"Archangel Gabriel.\" Regarded by most of Cairo's Kindred as the head of the city's Malkavians. His clanmate Assad Salhoum, a @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla}-loyal archon-informant, has drawn the attention of the Setite councilor Izzat al-Khunzir. Aziz, the Prince of Riddles, is a fellow Malkavian who has genuinely achieved Golconda and privately considers Nazrudin a deluded fraud.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
